<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81749" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέριξ</span></b> , strengthd. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί</span>, mostly 
			Ion.
		 Prose and Trag. (in latter usu. Adv.): <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> Prep., <i>round about, all
			round</i>, c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.179
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.8.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				2p.51U.
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> rarely
			c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				710
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> commonly c.
			acc., <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.196
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.158
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.36
			</span></i>, al.: mostly before its case, but also after, ib.<i><span class="en">
				52
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				79
			</span></i>, as also in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				368
			</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				243
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adv.
			<i>round about</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὑπορύσσοντες τὸ τεῖχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.115
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. λαβεῖν ἄνθρωπον</span> to
			surround him, ib.<i><span class="en">
				87
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκλῳ π</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				418
			</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1301
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				266
			</span></i> ; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠκεανὸς] π. γᾶν ἀμπέχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Limen.
					10
				</span></i>
			 : metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶν π. φρονοῦντες</span>
			<i>circuitously</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				448
			</span></i> : rare in 
				Att.
			 Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. πολιορκεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.90
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ π. τόπος, οἱ π</span>., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				62e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.5.2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				2p.47U.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ π. χρόνος</span>, i.e. all
			times save the present, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Int.</u>
				16b18
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π. ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Sens.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			 ; later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ π. πόλεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					5.16
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ π. κῶμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					880.44
				</span></i>
			 (Pizus, <span class="entity">iii A.D.</span>).</div>
